  "method": "One identical trivial memory-touching kernel (one aligned 16-byte load, one dependent integer op, one aligned 16-byte store per active thread) is timed two ways at the same grid and block: 64 separate launches into a stream, and the same 64 launches captured once into a CUDA graph and replayed. Both are warmed 200 rounds and the two modes alternate inside every trial so they see the same clock state. The published value is the minimum graph span across trials and rotations, so it is a floor rather than a typical duration, which is what composing by maximum requires.",
